pull_request.body:
This follow-up sharpens the article's opening after the compression pass.

Changes:
- removes the invented cache vignette;
- opens by linking directly to Naur's original *Programming as Theory Building* essay;
- states the research object as an automated system-building process rather than an unspecified "system";
- defines the target as a broad software factory made from the model, retained artifacts, tools, runtime, and correction machinery;
- shortens the later reintroduction of Naur's coherent-modification test.

The central question now asks whether an automated system-building process can hold and revise a fallible theory of the software it builds well enough to keep successive modifications coherent under delayed feedback.
